module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PowerPresentationSequences
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.NormInvertible.Generators
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TensorCoherence.Basic

/-!
# The elementary tensor of two local generators

Let `(X, 𝒪_X)` be a ringed space, let `L` and `M` be sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules and let `U` be an
open of `X`. A section `s ∈ L(U)` *generates* `L` on `U` when multiplication by `s` is a bijection
`𝒪_X(V) → L(V)` for every `V ≤ U` (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.GeneratorSections`). This file proves
that if `s` generates `L` on `U` and `t` generates `M` on `U`, then the image of `s ⊗ t` in the
tensor product sheaf generates `L ⊗_{𝒪_X} M` on `U`, and that the transition unit of two such
elementary tensors is the product of the transition units of the factors.

The second statement is the multiplicativity of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatorRatioUnit` across a tensor product. It is what the norm
construction of [Stacks, Tag 0BCY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCY) needs for the two
clauses that its well-definedness argument does not supply: additivity of the norm on Picard
groups, and the formula `Norm_f(f^* 𝒩) ≅ 𝒩^{⊗ d}`. In both of those the transition units of a
tensor product have to be read off the transition units of the factors, and that is exactly
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatorRatioUnit_tmulGenerator`.

## Which tensor product

The tensor product used is
`((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M`, the
sheafification of the objectwise tensor product (Tag 01CA). It is the tensor product in which
addition in `Stacks.SheafOfModules.PicardGroup` is defined
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_tensorSheaf`), so the results below apply to Picard classes
with no restatement and no bridging lemma.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatorEquiv` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatorCoordOfLE`: the
  trivialization of `L` on an open inside `U` given by a generator, and the coordinate of a local
  section in that frame.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tmulGenerator`: **the elementary tensor of two local generators, as a
  generator of the tensor product.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tmulGeneratorHom` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tmulGeneratorInv`:
  multiplication by that elementary tensor, and the pairing inverse to it, as mutually inverse
  morphisms of sheaves of modules on the slice site at `U`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_tmulGeneratorHom`: multiplication by the elementary tensor is an
  isomorphism `𝒪_U ≅ (L ⊗ M)|_U`. This is what makes `tmulGenerator` a generator.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tmulGenerator_restrict`: the elementary tensor of two generators commutes
  with restriction.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatorRatioUnit_tmulGenerator`: **the transition unit of two
  elementary tensors is the product of the transition units**,
  `[s⊗t : s'⊗t'] = [s : s'] · [t : t']`.

## Implementation notes

Multiplication by `s ⊗ t` is only defined over the opens inside `U`, so the isomorphism it
induces lives on the slice site at `U` rather than on `X`. The comparison between the restriction
of a tensor product and the tensor product of the restrictions is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorOver.tensorOverIso`, and its characterizing identity
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorOver.toSheafify_comp_tensorOverHom` is what lets the elementary
tensors be computed through it.

The inverse morphism is built by descent: the pairing `(a, b) ↦ a/s · b/t` is a bilinear family on
the objectwise tensor product, assembled by `PresheafOfModules.tensorMk`, and then extended along
the sheafification unit by the sheafification adjunction. That both composites are the identity is
checked on elementary tensors only — for one composite because the sections of the structure sheaf
on the slice site are generated by `1`, for the other because a morphism out of a sheafification
is determined by its restriction along the unit
(`PresheafOfModules.tensorObj_hom_ext` together with the injectivity of the adjunction's
`homEquiv`).

Two spelling choices are forced, because the alternatives do not elaborate. The scalars of a
module on the slice site are written `(RU U).obj.obj A`, never `X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left)`:
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf` is a plain `def`, so instance search
cannot see that the two agree, and `r • z` fails to synthesize in the second spelling. Conversely
every elementary tensor is written with its ring left to be determined by the expected type, since
the `Module` instance over the `X.presheaf` spelling is found only through the reducible
`structureSheafRing`. No `rw` is used in the construction of the bilinear pairing: all five of its
fields and its naturality are term-mode, which avoids the `implicit`-transparency failure that
`rw` meets on `(ov U L).val`.

A third spelling point concerns the sections of the tensor product itself, which are a module
over `(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj.obj V`.
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule` is the instance recovering `𝒪_X(V)` as
the scalar ring, so none is declared here. It is not *findable*, however:
its conclusion names the scalar ring `R.obj.obj V` for a variable `R`, so instance search would
have to solve `?R.obj =?= X.presheaf`, a projection applied to a metavariable. The four
declarations below that multiply a section of the tensor product therefore name that instance
locally. In the two whose *statements* multiply such a section, `tmulGenerator_smul` and
`toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul`, it is named by a `letI`, which inlines it, so that they are
exactly the propositions they would have been had search succeeded.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is placed: this is an ingredient of Tag 0BCY, not any clause of it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BCY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorOver
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} {U : Opens X.carrier}
  {L M : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)}

/-! ### The frame of a generator -/

/-- The trivialization of `L` over an open inside `U` determined by a generator over `U`. -/
noncomputable def generatorEquiv {U : Opens X.carrier}
    {L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)} (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U) :
    X.presheaf.obj (op V) ≃ₗ[X.presheaf.obj (op V)] L.val.obj (op V) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton _ _ (L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val)) (s.property V h)

/-- The inverse of the frame of a generator commutes with restriction to a smaller open. -/
theorem generatorEquiv_symm_restrict {U : Opens X.carrier}
    {L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)} (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    {V W : Opens X.carrier} (hV : V ≤ U) (hW : W ≤ V) (a : L.val.obj (op V)) :
    (generatorEquiv s (hW.trans hV)).symm (L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op a) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op ((generatorEquiv s hV).symm a) := by
  refine (generatorEquiv s (hW.trans hV)).injective ?_
  refine ((generatorEquiv s (hW.trans hV)).apply_symm_apply _).trans ?_
  have ha : a = (generatorEquiv s hV).symm a • L.val.map (homOfLE hV).op s.val :=
    ((generatorEquiv s hV).apply_symm_apply a).symm
  have hsmul : L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op
        ((generatorEquiv s hV).symm a • L.val.map (homOfLE hV).op s.val) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op ((generatorEquiv s hV).symm a) •
        L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op (L.val.map (homOfLE hV).op s.val) :=
    PresheafOfModules.map_smul L.val (homOfLE hW).op _ _
  have htrans : L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op (L.val.map (homOfLE hV).op s.val) =
      L.val.map (homOfLE (hW.trans hV)).op s.val :=
    (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply L.val (homOfLE hV).op (homOfLE hW).op s.val).symm.trans
      (PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply L.val (Subsingleton.elim _ _) _)
  exact (congrArg (fun z => (L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op) z) ha).trans
    (hsmul.trans (congrArg (fun z => (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op)
      ((generatorEquiv s hV).symm a) • z) htrans))

/-- The coordinate of a local section of `L` in the frame of a generator. -/
noncomputable def generatorCoordOfLE {U : Opens X.carrier}
    {L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X)} (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U) (a : L.val.obj (op V)) : X.presheaf.obj (op V) :=
  (generatorEquiv s h).symm a

/-- A local section is its coordinate times the restricted generator. -/
theorem generatorCoordOfLE_smul (s : GeneratorSections X L U) {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U)
    (a : L.val.obj (op V)) :
    generatorCoordOfLE s h a • L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val = a :=
  (generatorEquiv s h).apply_symm_apply a

/-- The coordinate in the frame of a generator is additive. -/
theorem generatorCoordOfLE_add (s : GeneratorSections X L U) {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U)
    (a a' : L.val.obj (op V)) :
    generatorCoordOfLE s h (a + a') = generatorCoordOfLE s h a + generatorCoordOfLE s h a' :=
  map_add (generatorEquiv s h).symm a a'

/-- The coordinate in the frame of a generator is linear over the structure sheaf. -/
theorem generatorCoordOfLE_smul_coeff (s : GeneratorSections X L U) {V : Opens X.carrier}
    (h : V ≤ U)
    (r : X.presheaf.obj (op V)) (a : L.val.obj (op V)) :
    generatorCoordOfLE s h (r • a) = r * generatorCoordOfLE s h a :=
  map_smul (generatorEquiv s h).symm r a

/-- The restricted generator has coordinate `1` in its own frame. -/
@[simp]
theorem generatorCoordOfLE_generator (s : GeneratorSections X L U) {V : Opens X.carrier}
    (h : V ≤ U) :
    generatorCoordOfLE s h (L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val) = 1 :=
  (generatorEquiv s h).injective
    (((generatorEquiv s h).apply_symm_apply _).trans (one_smul _ _).symm)

/-- The coordinate in the frame of a generator commutes with restriction. -/
theorem generatorCoordOfLE_restrict (s : GeneratorSections X L U) {V W : Opens X.carrier}
    (hV : V ≤ U) (hW : W ≤ V) (a : L.val.obj (op V)) :
    generatorCoordOfLE s (hW.trans hV) (L.val.map (homOfLE hW).op a) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op (generatorCoordOfLE s hV a) :=
  generatorEquiv_symm_restrict s hV hW a

/-! ### The pairing against two generators -/

/-- The pairing of two generators, as a morphism out of the objectwise tensor product on the
slice site at `U`: it sends `a ⊗ b` to the product of the coordinates of `a` and `b` in the two
frames. -/
noncomputable def tmulPairingPre (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (ov U L).val (ov U M).val ⟶
      (SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U)).val :=
  PresheafOfModules.tensorMk
    (fun A a b => generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a *
      generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b)
    (fun A a a' b =>
      (congrArg (fun z : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left) =>
          z * generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b)
        (generatorCoordOfLE_add s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a a')).trans (add_mul _ _ _))
    (fun A r a b =>
      (congrArg (fun z : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left) =>
          z * generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b)
        (generatorCoordOfLE_smul_coeff s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) r a)).trans (mul_assoc _ _ _))
    (fun A a b b' =>
      (congrArg (fun z : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left) =>
          generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a * z)
        (generatorCoordOfLE_add t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b b')).trans (mul_add _ _ _))
    (fun A r a b =>
      (congrArg (fun z : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left) =>
          generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a * z)
        (generatorCoordOfLE_smul_coeff t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) r b)).trans (mul_left_comm _ _ _))
    (fun {A B} f a b =>
      (map_mul (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (leOfHom ((Over.forget U).map f.unop))).op).hom
          (generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a)
          (generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b)).trans
        (congrArg₂ (fun y z : X.presheaf.obj (op B.unop.left) => y * z)
          (generatorCoordOfLE_restrict s (leOfHom A.unop.hom)
            (leOfHom ((Over.forget U).map f.unop)) a).symm
          (generatorCoordOfLE_restrict t (leOfHom A.unop.hom)
            (leOfHom ((Over.forget U).map f.unop)) b).symm))

/-- The pairing `tmulPairingPre` sends `a ⊗ b` to the product of the coordinates of `a` and `b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tmulPairingPre_tmul (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (tmulPairingPre s t) A (a ⊗ₜ b) =
      generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a * generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b :=
  rfl

/-- The pairing of two generators, as a morphism out of the tensor product formed on the slice
site at `U`. It is the extension of `tmulPairingPre` along the sheafification unit. -/
noncomputable def tmulPairingDesc (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨OU (X := X) U, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ (OU (X := X) U)
          (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) (hOU U)⟩).obj (ov U L)).obj (ov U M))
      ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U) :=
  ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)).homEquiv
    ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))
    (SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U))).symm (tmulPairingPre s t)

/-- The extension `tmulPairingDesc` restricts to `tmulPairingPre` along the sheafification unit. -/
theorem toSheafify_comp_tmulPairingDesc (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
        ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val)) ≫
      (SheafOfModules.forget (RU (X := X) U) ⋙
        PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 (RU (X := X) U).obj)).map (tmulPairingDesc s t) =
      tmulPairingPre s t :=
  ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU
    U)).homEquiv_unit
      (f := tmulPairingDesc s t)).symm.trans
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU
      U)).homEquiv _ _).apply_symm_apply _)

/-- The pairing `tmulPairingDesc` sends the image of `a ⊗ b` to the product of the coordinates of
`a` and `b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tmulPairingDesc_unit (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    (tmulPairingDesc s t).val.app A
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
          ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))).app A
            (a ⊗ₜ b)) =
      generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a * generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b :=
  (congrArg (fun h : (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := (OU (X := X) U)) ((ov U
    L).val) ((ov U M).val)) ⟶
        (SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U)).val =>
      PresheafOfModules.Hom.app h A (a ⊗ₜ b))
    (toSheafify_comp_tmulPairingDesc s t)).trans (tmulPairingPre_tmul s t A a b)

/-! ### The elementary tensor of two generators -/

/-- The elementary tensor of two local generators, as a section of the tensor product over the
open on which they are defined. -/
noncomputable def tmulGeneratorVal (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj (op U) :=
  toTensorSheafSection X L M (op U) (s.val ⊗ₜ t.val)

/-- The restriction of the elementary tensor of two generators to an open `V ≤ U` is the elementary
tensor of their restrictions. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorVal_restrict (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U) :
    (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.map (homOfLE h).op
        (tmulGeneratorVal s t) =
      toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V)
        (L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val ⊗ₜ M.val.map (homOfLE h).op t.val) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    (sheafifyUnit X (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := X.presheaf) L.val M.val))
    (homOfLE h).op (s.val ⊗ₜ t.val)).symm

/-- The elementary tensor of two local generators, as a global section of the tensor product on
the slice site at `U`. -/
noncomputable def tmulGeneratorSections (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk
    (fun A => (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.map
      (homOfLE (leOfHom A.unop.hom)).op (tmulGeneratorVal s t))
    (fun {A _} f =>
      (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply
            (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val
            (homOfLE (leOfHom A.unop.hom)).op
            (homOfLE (leOfHom ((Over.forget U).map f.unop))).op
            (tmulGeneratorVal s t)).symm.trans
        (PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply
          (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val
          (Subsingleton.elim _ _) (tmulGeneratorVal s t)))

/-- Multiplication by the elementary tensor of two generators, as a morphism from the structure
sheaf on the slice site at `U`. -/
noncomputable def tmulGeneratorHom (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U) ⟶
      ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) :=
  (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)).unitHomEquiv.symm
    (tmulGeneratorSections s t)

/-- On sections, `tmulGeneratorHom` is multiplication by the elementary tensor of the two
generators. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorHom_app (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (r : (RU (X := X) U).obj.obj A) :
    (tmulGeneratorHom s t).val.app A r = r • (tmulGeneratorSections s t).eval A :=
  rfl

/-- The pairing against the two generators, as a morphism back to the structure sheaf on the
slice site at `U`. -/
noncomputable def tmulGeneratorInv (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) ⟶
      SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U) :=
  (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).inv ≫ tmulPairingDesc s t

/-- The comparison `tensorOverIso` sends the image of `a ⊗ b` in the tensor product formed on the
slice site to its image in the restricted tensor product. -/
theorem tensorOverIso_hom_app_toSheafify (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ)
    (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom.val.app A
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
          ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))).app A
            (a ⊗ₜ b)) =
      toTensorSheafSection X L M (op A.unop.left) (a ⊗ₜ b) :=
  congrArg (fun h : (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val
        (ov U M).val) ⟶
      (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)).val =>
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app h A (a ⊗ₜ b))
    (toSheafify_comp_tensorOverHom (X := X) U L M)

/-- The inverse of `tensorOverIso` sends the image of `a ⊗ b` in the restricted tensor product to
its image in the tensor product formed on the slice site. -/
theorem tensorOverIso_inv_app_toTensorSheafSection (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ)
    (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).inv.val.app A
        (toTensorSheafSection X L M (op A.unop.left) (a ⊗ₜ b)) =
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
        (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val
          (ov U M).val)).app A (a ⊗ₜ b) :=
  (congrArg ((tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).inv.val.app A)
      (tensorOverIso_hom_app_toSheafify (U := U) A a b).symm).trans
    (congrArg (fun h :
          (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨OU (X := X) U, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _
              (OU (X := X) U) (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) (hOU U)⟩).obj (ov U L)).obj
                (ov U M)) ⟶
            (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨OU (X := X) U, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _
              (OU (X := X) U) (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) (hOU U)⟩).obj (ov U L)).obj
                (ov U M)) =>
        PresheafOfModules.Hom.app h.val A
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
            (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val
              (ov U M).val)).app A
              (a ⊗ₜ b)))
      (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom_inv_id)

/-- The pairing `tmulGeneratorInv` sends `a ⊗ b` to the product of the coordinates of `a` and
`b`. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorInv_app (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    (tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A
        (toTensorSheafSection X L M (op A.unop.left) (a ⊗ₜ b)) =
      generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a * generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b :=
  (congrArg ((tmulPairingDesc s t).val.app A)
      (tensorOverIso_inv_app_toTensorSheafSection (U := U) A a b)).trans
    (tmulPairingDesc_unit s t A a b)

/-- Scalars on the two factors of an elementary tensor multiply on its image in the tensor
product. -/
private theorem toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul_smul (V : Opens X.carrier)
    (c d : X.presheaf.obj (op V)) (a : L.val.obj (op V)) (b : M.val.obj (op V)) :
    letI : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
        ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
      fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
    toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V) ((c • a) ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op V)] (d • b)) =
      (c * d) • toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V) (a ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op V)] b) := by
  let : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
      ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
    fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul_smul]
  exact ((sheafifyUnit X (PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := X.presheaf) L.val
    M.val)).app (op V)).hom.map_smul _ _

/-- An elementary tensor `a ⊗ b` is the product of the coordinates of `a` and `b` times the
elementary tensor of the restricted generators. -/
theorem toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U)
    (a : L.val.obj (op V)) (b : M.val.obj (op V)) :
    letI : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
        ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
      fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
    (generatorCoordOfLE s h a * generatorCoordOfLE t h b) •
        toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V)
          (L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val ⊗ₜ M.val.map (homOfLE h).op t.val) =
      toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V) (a ⊗ₜ b) := by
  have key := toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul_smul (L := L) (M := M) V (generatorCoordOfLE s h a)
    (generatorCoordOfLE t h b) (L.val.map (homOfLE h).op s.val) (M.val.map (homOfLE h).op t.val)
  exact key.symm.trans (congrArg (toTensorSheafSection X L M (op V))
    (congrArg₂ (· ⊗ₜ[X.presheaf.obj (op V)] ·) (generatorCoordOfLE_smul s h a)
      (generatorCoordOfLE_smul t h b)))

/-- Multiplication by the elementary tensor, applied after the pairing, fixes every elementary
tensor `a ⊗ b`. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorHom_app_inv_app (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ)
    (a : (ov U L).val.obj A) (b : (ov U M).val.obj A) :
    (tmulGeneratorHom s t).val.app A ((tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A
        (toTensorSheafSection X L M (op A.unop.left) (a ⊗ₜ b))) =
      toTensorSheafSection X L M (op A.unop.left) (a ⊗ₜ b) :=
  let : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
      ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
    fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
  (congrArg ((tmulGeneratorHom s t).val.app A) (tmulGeneratorInv_app s t A a b)).trans
    ((tmulGeneratorHom_app s t A _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun z : (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj
              M).val.obj (op A.unop.left) =>
            (generatorCoordOfLE s (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a *
              generatorCoordOfLE t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) b) • z)
          (tmulGeneratorVal_restrict s t (leOfHom A.unop.hom))).trans
        (toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul s t (leOfHom A.unop.hom) a b)))

/-- The pairing sends the elementary tensor of the two generators to `1`. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorInv_app_sections (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) (A : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) :
    (tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A ((tmulGeneratorSections s t).eval A) =
      (1 : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left)) :=
  (congrArg ((tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A)
      (tmulGeneratorVal_restrict s t (leOfHom A.unop.hom))).trans
    ((tmulGeneratorInv_app s t A _ _).trans
      ((congrArg₂ (fun y z : X.presheaf.obj (op A.unop.left) => y * z)
          (generatorCoordOfLE_generator s (leOfHom A.unop.hom))
          (generatorCoordOfLE_generator t (leOfHom A.unop.hom))).trans (one_mul 1)))

/-- The pairing is a left inverse of multiplication by the elementary tensor. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorHom_comp_inv (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    tmulGeneratorHom s t ≫ tmulGeneratorInv s t =
      𝟙 (SheafOfModules.unit (RU (X := X) U)) := by
  ext A
  exact (congrArg ((tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A)
      ((tmulGeneratorHom_app s t A 1).trans (one_smul _ _))).trans
    (tmulGeneratorInv_app_sections s t A)

/-- The pairing is a right inverse of multiplication by the elementary tensor. -/
theorem tmulGeneratorInv_comp_hom (s : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    tmulGeneratorInv s t ≫ tmulGeneratorHom s t =
      𝟙 (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)) := by
  refine (Iso.cancel_iso_hom_left (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M) _ _).mp ?_
  refine ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU
    U)).homEquiv
    ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))
    (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M))).injective ?_
  refine PresheafOfModules.tensorObj_hom_ext (fun A a b => ?_)
  have hw := tensorOverIso_hom_app_toSheafify (U := U) (L := L) (M := M) A a b
  have hL : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU
          U)).homEquiv
            ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))
            (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)))
          ((tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom ≫
            tmulGeneratorInv s t ≫ tmulGeneratorHom s t)) A (a ⊗ₜ b) =
      (tmulGeneratorHom s t).val.app A ((tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A
        ((tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom.val.app A
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
            ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))).app A
              (a ⊗ₜ b)))) := rfl
  have hR : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.sheafifyAdjunction (OU (X := X) U) (hOU
          U)).homEquiv
            ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))
            (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)))
          ((tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom ≫
            𝟙 (ov U (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M)))) A (a ⊗ₜ b) =
      (tensorOverIso (X := X) U L M).hom.val.app A
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.toSheafify (OU (X := X) U) (hOU U)
          ((PresheafOfModules.tensorObj (O := OU (X := X) U) (ov U L).val (ov U M).val))).app A
            (a ⊗ₜ b)) := rfl
  refine hL.trans ((?_ : _ = _).trans hR.symm)
  exact (congrArg (fun z => (tmulGeneratorHom s t).val.app A
      ((tmulGeneratorInv s t).val.app A z)) hw).trans
    ((tmulGeneratorHom_app_inv_app s t A a b).trans hw.symm)

/-- **Multiplication by the elementary tensor of two generators is an isomorphism** between the
structure sheaf and the tensor product, on the slice site at `U`. -/
theorem isIso_tmulGeneratorHom (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    IsIso (tmulGeneratorHom s t) :=
  ⟨tmulGeneratorInv s t, tmulGeneratorHom_comp_inv s t, tmulGeneratorInv_comp_hom s t⟩

/-- **The elementary tensor of two local generators generates the tensor product.** -/
noncomputable def tmulGenerator (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    GeneratorSections X (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) U := by
  refine ⟨tmulGeneratorVal s t, fun V h => ?_⟩
  have := isIso_tmulGeneratorHom s t
  exact ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    ((SheafOfModules.forget (RU (X := X) U) ⋙
      PresheafOfModules.evaluation _ (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).mapIso
        (asIso (tmulGeneratorHom s t))).hom

/-- The section underlying `tmulGenerator s t` is the image of `s ⊗ t` in the tensor product. -/
@[simp]
theorem tmulGenerator_val (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    (tmulGenerator s t).val = toTensorSheafSection X L M (op U) (s.val ⊗ₜ t.val) :=
  rfl

/-- **The elementary tensor of two generators commutes with restriction.** -/
theorem tmulGenerator_restrict (s : GeneratorSections X L U) (t : GeneratorSections X M U)
    {V : Opens X.carrier} (h : V ≤ U) :
    generatorRestrict (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) h
        (tmulGenerator s t) =
      tmulGenerator (generatorRestrict L h s) (generatorRestrict M h t) :=
  Subtype.ext (tmulGeneratorVal_restrict s t h)

/-- Scaling the two generators scales their elementary tensor by the product. -/
theorem tmulGenerator_smul (s s' : GeneratorSections X L U) (t t' : GeneratorSections X M U)
    (c d : X.presheaf.obj (op U)) (hs : s'.val = c • s.val) (ht : t'.val = d • t.val) :
    letI : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
        ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
      fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
    (tmulGenerator s' t').val = (c * d) • (tmulGenerator s t).val := by
  change toTensorSheafSection X L M (op U) (s'.val ⊗ₜ t'.val) = _
  rw [hs, ht]
  exact toTensorSheafSection_smul_tmul_smul U c d s.val t.val

/-- **Multiplicativity of the generator ratio across a tensor product**: the transition unit of
two elementary tensors of generators is the product of the transition units of the factors. -/
theorem generatorRatioUnit_tmulGenerator (s s' : GeneratorSections X L U)
    (t t' : GeneratorSections X M U) :
    generatorRatioUnit (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) U
        (tmulGenerator s t) (tmulGenerator s' t') =
      generatorRatioUnit L U s s' * generatorRatioUnit M U t t' := by
  let : ∀ W : (Opens X.carrier)ᵒᵖ, Module (X.presheaf.obj W)
      ((((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M).val.obj W) :=
    fun W ↦ Tensor.ringSheafSectionModule ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩ W _
  refine generatorRatioUnit_eq (((Tensor.sheafTensor ⟨X.presheaf, X.IsSheaf⟩).obj L).obj M) U
    (tmulGenerator s t) (tmulGenerator s' t')
    (generatorRatioUnit L U s s' * generatorRatioUnit M U t t') ?_
  refine (tmulGenerator_smul s s' t t' (generatorRatio L U s s') (generatorRatio M U t t')
    (generatorRatio_spec L U s s') (generatorRatio_spec M U t t')).trans ?_
  exact congrArg (fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op U) => c • (tmulGenerator s t).val)
    (congrArg₂ (fun y z : X.presheaf.obj (op U) => y * z)
      (generatorRatioUnit_val L U s s').symm (generatorRatioUnit_val M U t t').symm)

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

